From 55a5fc489e999083bfb68b3081f709999835aab6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:01:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] ipa: simple: Add autofocus algorithm

Add an Af algorithm to the software ISP IPA, built on the libipa
AfContrast algorithm and the focus statistics of the software ISP.

The contrast of each focus region is the mean squared green difference,
normalised by the square of the mean level above black of the whole
statistics window. This keeps the measurement independent of the
exposure, without giving flat regions as much weight as textured ones.
Lens positions computed by the algorithm are sent to the pipeline
handler with the sensor controls.

The algorithm only registers the autofocus controls when the camera has
a focus lens, and otherwise only reports FocusFoM. Enable it in the
uncalibrated tuning file.

[backport: moved to the simple IPA of v0.7.2, in src/ipa/simple and the
 ipa::soft namespace]

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
